# This repo holds the chezmoi source tree and documentation. There is no build
# output and no language toolchain, so this file stays minimal on purpose.
#
# It used to carry the full Python boilerplate from a Python project that was
# never written (the `arch_configurator` package REQUIREMENTS.md described;
# chezmoi does that job instead). That cost real work: its bare `var/` and
# `lib/` rules silently swallowed the managed system tree at
# dotfiles/system/var/lib/noctalia-greeter/, so greeter.toml was invisible to
# git and never reached the other machines, and re-include rules had to be
# added to undo it. Do not paste a language boilerplate in here again.

# Editor and agent local state
.vscode
.claude

# lazy.nvim writes this lockfile next to the config it manages
lazy-lock.json

# macOS Finder droppings (this tree is deployed on the MacBook too)
.DS_Store
